  "title": "The Glymphatic System: Brain Cleanup Crew",
  "emoji": "😴",
  "color": "#4C1D95",
  "description": "A short lesson to help you apply The Glymphatic System: Brain Cleanup Crew.",
  "is_free": false,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "Your brain produces toxic waste all day. The cleanup crew only works the night shift.",
      "visual": "🌙"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "The glymphatic system is a waste-clearance network that flushes cerebrospinal fluid through brain tissue.",
      "visual": "🚿"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "During deep sleep, brain cells shrink by 60%, widening channels so fluid can wash away debris.",
      "visual": "💧"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "One key toxin removed is beta-amyloid—the protein that builds up in Alzheimer's disease.",
      "visual": "🧬"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "Poor sleep means poor cleanup, which may explain the link between chronic insomnia and dementia.",
      "visual": "⚠️"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "Sleep is your brain's nightly power wash. Skip it and the grime builds up.",
      "visual": "🧽"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "What happens to brain cells during deep sleep to aid waste clearance?",
    "options": [
      "They shrink by about 60%",
      "They double in size",
      "They stop all electrical activity"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
